    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance visible from both directions on the street.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with posts or reflectors on both sides to define the entry point for responding units arriving at speed.\n• Keep the full width of the access drive clear of parked vehicles, equipment, and debris so emergency vehicles can reach the structure without stopping.\n• Trim any vegetation along the driveway edges that narrows the travel width or blocks driver sightlines.\n• Create a dedicated turnaround area near the structure large enough for a fire or rescue vehicle to reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Mark the turnaround area clearly so arriving crews can identify it immediately on approach.\n• Keep scattered vegetation near the structure trimmed back so it does not block walking paths around the building or access to exterior doors and utility shutoffs.\n• Maintain a clear path from the driveway to each exterior door so crews on foot can move directly to entry points without navigating around plantings or obstacles.\n• Keep the landscaped area immediately around the structure free of tall, dense, or overhanging plantings that would slow crew movement or block visibility of the structure from the driveway."
  },
