    "recommendations": "• Thin trees within the cluster closest to the structure to open up space between individual trees.\n• Remove shrubs growing directly against or immediately next to the structure.\n• Trim low-hanging branches on trees near the structure so branches do not extend close to the roofline or walls.\n• Cut and remove brush in the brush area nearest to the structure.\n• Mow or cut grass surrounding the structure, particularly during dry periods when grass is brown or dry.\n• Thin scattered shrubs within the mixed vegetation area closest to the structure to break up continuous plant coverage near the building.\n• Keep the long driveway clear of overhanging branches along its full length to allow emergency vehicle access.\n• Keep the driveway surface clear of brush and overgrown vegetation along both sides that could close in over the travel lane.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is easy to locate from the main road, particularly for emergency responders using the single access route.\n• Maintain the open terrain areas around the structure by preventing shrubs and grass from re-establishing in those cleared zones.\n• Remove dead or dry plant material from within the mixed vegetation area directly surrounding the structure.\n• Separate any wood piles, outdoor furniture, or stored materials from shrubs and vegetation growing nearby."
